# Tells Cloudflare which files in this folder are NOT part of the public
# website — so it only ever publishes index.html (the actual dashboard) and
# quietly ignores everything else in this repo (source code, notes, helper
# scripts). Uses the same kind of pattern rules as a .gitignore file.
#
# The most important two lines are .git and .wrangler — without this file,
# Cloudflare's last build was actually uploading raw pieces of this
# project's git history and build-tool internals as if they were public
# web pages. Nobody could reach anything sensitive through them (there's no
# password or key stored in git), but there's no reason to publish them
# either, so this shuts that off.

.git
.wrangler
node_modules

# Source code / config — read by Cloudflare to build the site, never
# meant to be visited directly in a browser.
src
wrangler.jsonc

# Everything below is project material that isn't part of the TV
# dashboard itself (Mac helper scripts, the old Netlify version, the
# Google Apps Script sync tool, scratch notes) — kept in this repo for
# convenience, not meant to be public web pages.
functions
netlify
netlify.toml
scratch
*.command
*.gs
cloudflare-worker.js
